What if kubectl freezes?
 🧪 Check API health with curl <api>/healthz
 🔐 Validate token/context
 🧠 For self-managed: SSH into control plane & check kubelet, etcd, apiserver logs
 🛟 On EKS: check VPC, ENI, or IAM token issues

2️⃣ Can you fix a stuck rollout with kubectl rollout undo?
 ✅ Yes, if the previous revision exists
 🧰 Else, check:
kubectl describe pod for CrashLoop, bad probes, secrets
Use kubectl patch or set image to roll forward safely
 💡 Don't rely only on undo — be ready to hotfix in-place

3️⃣ What if staging works, but prod breaks?
 ⚠️ Classic case of env drift
 🔍 Compare kubectl get all -o yaml in both envs
 🛠️ Check IAM, secrets, env vars, DNS, HPA, resource limits
 🧪 Use helm diff and GitOps tools to avoid drift

4️⃣ Fastest way to trace pod-to-pod latency?
 🚀 Use kubectl debug or ephemeral containers with netshoot
 🔎 Run ping, curl -w, traceroute, or mtr
 📈 On Istio/Cilium? Use istioctl, cilium monitor, or linkerd top

5️⃣ Node is NotReady but kubelet logs are clean?
 📦 Check:
Disk pressure/OOM via kubectl describe node
CNI plugin logs (Calico/Cilium)
Node OS logs: journalctl -u kubelet

 ✅ Drain & recycle if needed, especially in AWS/GKE managed nodes
